<style>
  .sbFaq1{max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;padding:8px 16px 24px;font-family:var(--font-body--family)}
  .sbFaq1-list{border-top:1px solid #eee}
  .sbFaq1-item{border-bottom:1px solid #eee;border-left:2px solid transparent;padding-left:0;transition:border-color .2s,padding-left .2s}
  .sbFaq1-item.open{border-left:2px solid #B5557F;padding-left:12px}
  .sbFaq1-q{width:100%;background:0;border:0;padding:15px 0;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:#1a1a1a;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-family:inherit}
  .sbFaq1-q:hover{color:#B5557F}
  .sbFaq1-item.open .sbFaq1-q{color:#B5557F}
  .sbFaq1-plus{font-size:22px;font-weight:300;color:#999;flex-shrink:0;transition:transform .2s,color .2s;line-height:1}
  .sbFaq1-item.open .sbFaq1-plus{transform:rotate(45deg);color:#B5557F}
  .sbFaq1-a{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height .35s ease}
  .sbFaq1-item.open .sbFaq1-a{max-height:800px}
  .sbFaq1-a-inner{padding:0 0 16px;font-size:14px;color:#666;line-height:1.6}
  .sbFaq1-a-inner strong{color:#1a1a1a}
  .sbFaq1-a-inner p{margin:0 0 10px}
  .sbFaq1-a-inner p:last-child{margin:0}
</style>
<div class="sbFaq1">
  <div class="sbFaq1-list">

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">Which size should I order?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p>Go by your <strong>waist measurement</strong>, not your usual clothing size. After a baby the two often stop matching, and that's exactly who this is made for.</p>
        <p>Measure around the <strong>narrowest part of your torso</strong>, a couple of inches above your belly button, keeping the tape level. If you're postpartum, measure <strong>above</strong> the fullest part of your belly, not across it. Then match it to the size chart.</p>
        <p>Between two sizes? <strong>Size up.</strong> The range runs from S all the way up to 5XL. Not sure? The <strong>Size Calculator</strong> on this page does it for you in ten seconds.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">Will it roll down or slide like other shapewear?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p>No, and there are two reasons why. The wide <strong>360&deg; crossed band</strong> wraps all the way around, front, sides and back, so the hold is spread evenly instead of pressing on one spot.</p>
        <p>On top of that, the waistband has an <strong>integrated silicone gripper and anti-roll ribbing</strong> that keeps it exactly where you put it. It stays put through a full day, even when you sit. No rolling down, no riding up, no readjusting in the bathroom.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">Will it show under my clothes?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p>No. The fabric is thin and <strong>bonded rather than stitched</strong>, so there are no bulky seams to print through, and the leg openings are finished as <strong>no-show lines</strong> instead of elastic bands that cut in and leave a ridge.</p>
        <p>It disappears under fitted dresses, jeans, leggings and work clothes. Smooth lines, every time.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">What is it made of?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p><strong>83% polyamide (nylon), 17% spandex</strong>, with breathable mesh panels and a <strong>cotton-lined gusset</strong>. That blend is the whole reason it doesn't feel like stiff, plasticky shapewear.</p>
        <p>The <strong>nylon</strong> is what makes it thin, silky and <strong>breathable</strong>, so it stays invisible under clothes and doesn't trap heat through a full day. It's also what keeps it second-skin soft on sensitive, healing skin.</p>
        <p>The <strong>spandex</strong> is what gives it real compression <strong>with recovery</strong>. It holds you firmly, moves with you when you sit, bend and lift your baby, then snaps straight back to shape instead of going slack after a few wears.</p>
        <p><strong>No latex, no hard boning, no plastic edges digging in.</strong></p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">Do I wear it over my underwear or on its own?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p><strong>Either way works, it's completely your choice.</strong> Most women wear it on its own, exactly like regular underwear, and it's built for that: the gusset is <strong>lined with cotton</strong>, so it's soft, breathable and hygienic against the skin all day, just like your normal pair.</p>
        <p>If you'd rather wear a thin pair underneath, that's <strong>absolutely fine too</strong> and it changes nothing about the shaping or the hold. There is no wrong answer here, just whatever feels most comfortable to you.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">Do I have to wear it every day?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p>You don't have to, but <strong>daily is where the difference comes from.</strong> Most women wear it a few hours a day, or right through the day, because steady, consistent support does far more than wearing it now and then.</p>
        <p><strong>Miss a day and nothing is ruined.</strong> But if you're going to give it a real shot, make it part of getting dressed in the morning. It's soft enough that you genuinely forget it's on.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">Can I wear it at night?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p>You can, but <strong>you don't need to.</strong> It's made for daytime wear, and most women get their hours in during the day then give their body a break overnight.</p>
        <p>Some find it comfy enough to keep on for a nap or an evening on the sofa, and that's perfectly fine. <strong>The only rule: it should always feel supportive, never restrictive.</strong> If it ever feels too tight to relax in, take it off.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">When can I wear it after birth, including after a C-section?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">Most women start around <strong>2 weeks after a vaginal birth</strong> and <strong>6 weeks after a C-section</strong>, once they've been cleared. It's soft and seamless with no hard boning. If you're recovering from surgery, check with your provider first.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">I had my baby years ago (5, 10, even 20+ years). Will it still work for me?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">
        <p>Yes, and here's the part almost no one explains: the gap pregnancy leaves in your abdominal wall <strong>doesn't close on its own with time</strong>. If your lower belly still pushes forward years later, it's because those muscles are simply <strong>still separated</strong>, which is exactly what the <strong>360&deg; crossed band</strong> is built to hold and support, all the way around.</p>
        <p>That's why it works whether you gave birth last year or decades ago. Our customers wear it from <strong>days after birth to decades postpartum</strong>. It was never about how long ago. Time was never going to fix it on its own, which is why <strong>it's never too late to start</strong>.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">How do I wash it?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">Machine wash cold on a gentle cycle in a laundry bag, or hand wash, then <strong>air dry</strong>. No tumble dryer, no fabric softener. That's what keeps the spandex firm and the hold exactly as it was on day one.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sbFaq1-item">
      <button class="sbFaq1-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">How soon will I see a difference, and what if it's not for me?<span class="sbFaq1-plus">+</span></button>
      <div class="sbFaq1-a"><div class="sbFaq1-a-inner">You'll look <strong>flat and smooth under clothes the moment you put it on</strong>. With daily wear, most women say their midsection feels firmer within 2 to 3 weeks. And it's backed by a <strong>90-day fit guarantee</strong>: wear it, and if it's not right for you, just reach out and we'll make it right, with a size exchange or your money back.</div></div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

